CISO (Chief information security officer)
Oversees the whole information security program

Security Architect
Designs secure networks and systems

Penetration Tester
Finds, exploits and reports vulnerabilities in a system ethically

Incident Response Specialist
Manages and responses to security incidents

Security Analyst
Monitors systems for weaknesses and mitigates them

Compliance Specialist
Ensures that the organisation is complying to the standards and regulations

Blue Team
This team is responsible of internet security and responses to attacks

Red Team
This team simulates real attacks on systems ethically by permission

Purple Team
This team consists of blue and red teams working together to enhance the organizations security

Confidentiality
Ensures unauthorized people can't access the information and information systems
Protects against disclosure
Implemented through encryption and access controls

Integrity
Prevents unauthorized and incorrect modification or destruction of data.
Implemented through measures like hashing and digital signatures

Availability
Ensures data is available anytime for the one trying to access it
Prevents disruption
Implemented through redundancy and disaster recovery planning

Non-Repudiation
Ensures that a party cannot deny the message or email originated from them
used in e-commerce and legal contexts
Implemented through digital signatures and audit logs

Authentication
verifies the identity of a person, system or a device
Integral for authorization
Implemented through passwords, biometrics, mfa

Privacy
Focuses on correctly handling sensitive information by complying to data protection regulations	
Implemented through data minimization and consent management

Data Minimization
Process of storing, processing, using only the necessary amount of personal information for a specific purpose

Consent Management
Is a system or process that users can choose and determine the information they are willing to permit to their various providers access
